page RecipeActiveTabInTheAddress(path: "/recipes/active-tab-in-the-address", title: "Keep the active tab in the address — Recipes", description: "Keep the active tab in the address's #fragment, so it survives a reload and a shared link opens on the same tab.") {
    RecipeShell("Keep the active tab in the address", summary: "A tab held in a `state` goes back to the first one on every reload. To make the tab survive a reload, and a shared link open on the same tab, read it from the address's `#fragment`:", outputs: ["website", "app"], since: "", recipes: RECIPE_INDEX, sections: [Anchor(id: "how-it-works", label: "How it works")], related: [RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Keep filters in the address", to: "/recipes/filters-in-the-address"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Build a confirm dialog", to: "/recipes/confirm-dialog"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Copy to the clipboard", to: "/recipes/copy-to-the-clipboard")], source: "md-docs/recipes/active-tab-in-the-address.md", how: true, hasVariations: false, project: { "src/pages/ActiveTabInTheAddress.wf": #"page Account(path: "/account", title: "Account", description: "Your profile and billing.") {
    derived tab = if hash != "" { hash } else { "profile" }
    Heading("Account").h1
    Tabs(value: tab, label: "Account") {
        on change(v) { navigate("/account#{v}") }
        Tabs.Page("Profile", value: "profile") { Text("Profile settings") }
        Tabs.Page("Billing", value: "billing") { Text("Billing settings") }
    }
}
"#, "webfluent.app.json": #"{
  "name": "active-tab-in-the-address"
}
"# }) {
        code {
            CodeBlock(#"page Account(path: "/account", title: "Account", description: "Your profile and billing.") {
    derived tab = if hash != "" { hash } else { "profile" }
    Heading("Account").h1
    Tabs(value: tab, label: "Account") {
        on change(v) { navigate("/account#{v}") }
        Tabs.Page("Profile", value: "profile") { Text("Profile settings") }
        Tabs.Page("Billing", value: "billing") { Text("Billing settings") }
    }
}"#, title: "wf")
        }
        Markdown("Open `/account#billing` and the Billing tab is selected; click Profile and the address becomes `/account#profile`.\n\n- [`hash`](/learn/05-pages-and-routing#query-strings-and-fragments) is the address's fragment without the `#`, kept current by the runtime.\n- `tab` is a [`derived`](/learn/07-state-and-reactivity#derived) value: the fragment when there is one, `\"profile\"` when there is none.\n- `Tabs(value: tab)` opens the page whose `value:` is `tab`. It only reads it: picking a tab fires `on change(v)` with that page's value, which navigates to the same page with another fragment. `hash` changes, `tab` follows, and the tab opens. Each pick is a step in the history, so the back button steps through the tabs the reader opened.\n- The tabs are a tab list to a screen reader, each linked to its panel. Only the open tab is in the Tab order; the arrow keys move between tabs (the other way round in a right-to-left page), and Home and End go to the ends.\n\nFor a tab that need not survive a reload, `Tabs(bind: tab)` reads and writes a `state` instead.\n\nWhy not a `Link` per tab? The router marks a link current by its path, not its fragment: on `/account#billing`, both `/account#profile` and `/account#billing` are links to the current page, so both get the `active` class and `aria-current=\"page\"`, and neither the look nor a screen reader says which tab is open.\n\nTo keep several settings in the address, such as a sort and a filter, use the query string instead: see [Keep filters in the address](/recipes/filters-in-the-address).")

    }
}
